                <head>Chapter VII: March 13–31, 1932</head>
                <p>First Meeting Between Chinese and Japanese To Discuss Shanghai Armistice, March
                    14; British Statement of Policy Respecting Far East, March 22; Extension of
                    Japanese Military Control Along Chinese Eastern Railway and Sungari River; First
                    Formal Session of Shanghai Armistice Negotiators, March 24; “Independence” of
                    Chinese Salt Revenue Administration in Manchuria, March 28; Japanese
                    Interference With Chinese Postal Service in Manchuria</p>















































































